From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: lpass-macro: force runtime suspend across system sleep

The LPASS RX/TX/VA/WSA macros only have runtime PM ops. On the AYN Odin 3
the WCD9390 SoundWire peripherals are kept runtime-active, so the
SoundWire masters and the macros they clock stay active through s2idle.
The macros then keep their q6prm clock and HW macro/dcodec votes, the
ADSP keeps LPASS powered, and its RPMh DRV ("AUDIO" in the AOP CXPC
violator log) blocks CX power collapse for the whole sleep.

Force the runtime suspend across system sleep so the votes, which the
PM clock framework conversion now releases in runtime suspend, are
dropped for s2idle as well.

Taken from ArmadaOS (packages/kernel/patches/0563).

---
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
index c4c9a08c9..d89002cdd 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
@@ -4094,6 +4094,7 @@ static int rx_macro_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops rx_macro_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(rx_macro_runtime_suspend, rx_macro_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
index 25a35d69b..78a8944a5 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-tx-macro.c
@@ -2449,6 +2449,7 @@ static int tx_macro_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops tx_macro_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(tx_macro_runtime_suspend, tx_macro_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
index cd9c68978..06910d1ac 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
@@ -1807,6 +1807,7 @@ static int va_macro_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops va_macro_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
